I've always read that  <<- is bad form, unless you have a very good reason to use it.

Also, the code in the form that I posted it is only one incarnation that doesn't work.  I first tried to assign the variable vals to a reactiveValue in the server environment, with something like

 vals <- reactiveValues(
      keeprows = if(!is.null(mydata())) rep(TRUE, nrow(mydata())
   )

which is a straightforward extension of the shiny gallery example, but using my own data frame rather than mtcars.  However, that fails immediately, giving:

Error in .getReactiveEnvironment()$currentContext() :
  Operation not allowed without an active reactive context. (You tried to do something that can only be done from inside a reactive expression or observer.)

I have determined that the error in this particular case is in "nrow(mydata())".  Apparently there is a rule that you can't use a regular R expression on a reactive expression unless you are inside another reactive expression.

On the other hand, Isolate() says it is supposed to return a regular R expression from a reactive expression, but I get the same " Operation not allowed without an active reactive context" error message if I try using isolate.

